 "storage": "Better on day two than day one and keeps 4 days in the fridge, where it will set to a soft jelly and loosen again the moment it is warmed. Freezes well for 3 months. ⚠️ Reheat it gently and stirred as little as possible — a hard reheat breaks the cubes up in a way the long simmer never did.",
 "chefNotes": "⚖️ Make it the day before. This is not a nice-to-have with a pot like this — the seasoning is still sitting mostly in the liquid when the cooking time is up, and a night in the fridge is what moves it into the meat.\n\n✅ Big cubes, and resist cutting them smaller. Three centimetres looks excessive raw and is exactly right after two hours.\n\n⚠️ Star anise is stronger than it looks and it is the flavour that takes this dish over the line into tasting like a spice cabinet. One whole star for a pot this size, and pull it out the moment the time is up.\n\n⛔ Never salt this at the start to where it tastes right at the start. Half the water in the pot will still be there at the end, so a broth seasoned correctly at minute one is a broth seasoned correctly at minute one and nowhere else.",
